<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sabah I bin Jaber</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1762</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabah">Sabah</a> I bin Jaber was the first ruler of Kuwait, chosen as leader around 1752 by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bani-utbah">Bani Utbah</a> families who had settled on the bay. He handled relations with the Ottoman authorities in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basra">Basra</a> and the surrounding tribes, while the town lived from trade, pearling and shipbuilding. His descendants, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-sabah">Al Sabah</a>, have ruled Kuwait ever since.</p></div>
